---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="SamoSpec — git-native AI spec authoring">
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Turn a rough idea into a reviewed, versioned spec.</h1>
    <p class="tagline">
      <code>samospec</code> runs a panel of top AI models against your idea: a
      <strong>lead</strong> drafts, two <strong>reviewers</strong> critique with
      different personas, the lead revises, and the loop repeats until convergence.
      The result is <code>SPEC.md</code> with real commit history you can diff and
      blame.
    </p>
    <a class="cta" href="#install">bunx samospec doctor →</a>
  </section>

  <section id="install">
    <h2>Install</h2>
    <p>
      Requires <a href="https://bun.sh">Bun</a> ≥ 1.2. <code>bunx</code> fetches
      and caches the CLI on first use — no install step.
    </p>
    <pre><code>bunx samospec doctor
bunx samospec --version</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section id="quickstart">
    <h2>Quickstart</h2>
    <p>Three commands, from idea to reviewed spec:</p>
    <pre><code>bunx samospec init
bunx samospec new linkrot --idea "Detect dead links in Markdown files"
bunx samospec iterate linkrot
bunx samospec publish linkrot</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section id="how">
    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <pre><code>                 ┌────────────────────┐
   idea  ──►     │  LEAD  (Claude)    │  ──►   SPEC.md v0.N
                 │  draft / revise    │
                 └────┬───────────────┘
                      │  (parallel)
       ┌──────────────┴──────────────┐
       ▼                             ▼
 ┌──────────────┐             ┌──────────────┐
 │ Reviewer A   │             │ Reviewer B   │
 │ (Codex)      │             │ (Claude #2)  │
 │ security/ops │             │ QA/pedant    │
 └──────┬───────┘             └───────┬──────┘
        │                             │
        └───────┐             ┌───────┘
                ▼             ▼
             ┌──────────────────────┐
             │  round.json          │  ─► commit ─► repeat
             │  claude.md, codex.md │
             │  decisions.md update │
             └──────────────────────┘</code></pre>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Lead</strong> = <code>claude</code> CLI, pinned <code
          >claude-opus-4-7</code
        >, effort <code>max</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Reviewer A</strong> = <code>codex</code> CLI, security/ops
        persona.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Reviewer B</strong> = a second Claude session, QA/testability
        persona.
      </li>
      <li>
        Every round is a commit on the <code>samospec/&lt;slug&gt;</code> branch.
        <code>git log</code> tells the story.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="demo">
    <h2>Live demo</h2>
    <p>
      A real spec produced end-to-end over ChatGPT-account OAuth — 7 review
      rounds, both reviewers writing real critiques:
    </p>
    <p>
      → <a
        href="https://github.com/NikolayS/todo-stream/tree/samospec/todo-stream"
        >NikolayS/todo-stream <code>samospec/todo-stream</code> branch</a
      >
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="publish">
    <h2>Publish to the web</h2>
    <p>
      Push a finished <code>SPEC.md</code> to samospec.dev to share a tidy,
      read-only URL — optionally gated by a 6-character access code:
    </p>
    <pre><code>bunx samospec publish linkrot --web
# → https://samospec.dev/s/k8m3qr2x
# → access code: 7K2P9M</code></pre>
    <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.92rem">
      Publishing-to-web is opt-in per spec; nothing leaves your machine without <code
        >--web</code
      >. Specs without a code are publicly viewable at the URL.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
